{"slug":"echium-vulgare","plant":{"taxon":"Echium vulgare","family":"Boraginaceae","rank":"species","gbif_key":2925892,"wikidata":"Q157722","iucn":null,"gbif_occurrences":461293,"common_name":"viper's bugloss","names":[{"source":"culpeper","name":"Viper’S Bugloss","monograph_id":"cul:319-vipers-bugloss","confidence":"high","note":"Rough prickly stalks; viper's bugloss."}],"n_compounds":15,"top_compounds":[{"name":"beta-sitosterol","qid":"Q121802"},{"name":"gamolenic acid","qid":"Q415885"},{"name":"echimidine","qid":"Q27106462"},{"name":"heliosupine","qid":"Q27106842"},{"name":"uplandicine","qid":"Q27108507"},{"name":"echinatine","qid":"Q27266232"},{"name":"(9E,12Z)-linoleic acid","qid":"Q27285202"},{"name":"2-Butenoic acid, 2-methyl-, 7-[[2,3-dihydroxy-2-(1-hydroxyethyl)-3-methyl-1-oxobutoxy]methyl]-2,3,5,7a-tetrahydro-1H-pyrrolizin-1-yl ester","qid":"Q104250297"}],"epmc_total":81,"trials":0,"claims":[{"concept_id":"envenomation","dsc":0,"cul":2,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.95,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"heart","dsc":0,"cul":2,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.18,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"melancholy","dsc":0,"cul":2,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":1,"lift":0.85,"evidence_tier":"sparse"},{"concept_id":"fever","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":1,"lift":1.45,"evidence_tier":"sparse"},{"concept_id":"kidney_disease","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.39,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"lactation","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.75,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"poisoning","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":3,"lift":4.28,"evidence_tier":"sparse"}],"lead_score":null},"texts":{"cul:319-vipers-bugloss":{"ref":"Culpeper, Complete Herbal: Viper’s Bugloss","headword":"Viper’s Bugloss","lang":"en","source":"culpeper","text":"It is a most gallant herb of the Sun; it is a pity it is no more in use than it is. It is an especial remedy against the biting of the Viper, and all other venomous beasts, or serpents; as also against poison, or poisonous herbs. Dioscorides and others say, That whosoever shall take of the herb or root before they be bitten, shall not be hurt by the poison of any serpent. The root or seed is thought to be most effectual to comfort the heart, and expel sadness, or causeless melancholy; it tempers the blood, and allays hot fits of agues. The seed drank in wine, procures abundance of milk in women’s breasts. The same also being taken, eases the pains in the loins, back, and kidneys. The distilled water of the herb when it is in flower, or its chief strength, is excellent to be applied either inwardly or outwardly, for all the griefs aforesaid. There is a syrup made hereof very effectual for the comforting the heart, and expelling sadness and melancholy.","spans":[{"start":121,"end":130,"concept_id":"envenomation","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":135,"end":140,"concept_id":"envenomation","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":156,"end":164,"concept_id":"envenomation","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":176,"end":184,"concept_id":"envenomation","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":202,"end":208,"concept_id":"poisoning","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":213,"end":228,"concept_id":"poisoning","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":319,"end":325,"concept_id":"envenomation","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":427,"end":444,"concept_id":"heart","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":456,"end":463,"concept_id":"melancholy","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":523,"end":531,"concept_id":"fever","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":535,"end":540,"concept_id":"fever","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":566,"end":592,"concept_id":"lactation","polarity":"action"},{"start":680,"end":687,"concept_id":"kidney_disease","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":905,"end":925,"concept_id":"heart","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":941,"end":948,"concept_id":"melancholy","polarity":"therapeutic"}]}},"gloss":{"cul:319-vipers-bugloss":{"121":"biting / stinging of (serpents, scorpions, beasts)","135":"serpents, vipers, adders, scorpions, wasps","156":"venomous beasts / creatures","176":"serpents, vipers, adders, scorpions, wasps","202":"resists / expels poison","213":"poisonous herbs / qualities","319":"bitten or stung","352":"poison of any serpent","427":"comforts / strengthens / defends the heart","456":"sadness","523":"hot fits of agues","535":"agues: intermittent fevers","566":"increases milk: galactagogue","680":"kidneys","905":"comforts / strengthens / defends the heart","941":"sadness"}},"images":[]}